"""Colm O'Driscoll, part A: biography (Origins, Red Dead Redemption 2 chapters 1 to 4 and 6).

Sources (Red Dead Wiki EN, Oct 2026, saved in scratchpad cov/colm/ and cov/colm/m/): character page "Colm O'Driscoll"
(Background, Events, quote box, references); pages "O'Driscoll Boys", "Annabelle", "O'Driscoll Captured" (newspaper
text), "Letter to Tom from Colm" (letter text), "Tom (RDR2)", "Jake Adler"; transcripts "Outlaws from the West/dialogues",
"Old Friends/dialogues", "Who the Hell is Leviticus Cornwall?/dialogues", "The Aftermath of Genesis/dialogues",
"Blessed are the Peacemakers/dialogues" (parley, guards' talk, Colm and Arthur in the cabin, return to Clemens Point);
mission pages "Outlaws from the West", "Old Friends", "Who the Hell is Leviticus Cornwall?", "Paying a Social Call",
"Blessed are the Meek?", "An American Pastoral Scene", "Blessed are the Peacemakers" (location Lone Mule Stead, Big
Valley; gold medal objectives), "Horsemen, Apocalypses", "Icarus and Friends", "Goodbye, Dear Friend",
"Mrs. Sadie Adler, Widow" (I and II); wiki page "Camp Events" (Dutch and Micah's account after the capture).
No transcript exists on the wiki for "Goodbye, Dear Friend", "Horsemen, Apocalypses", "Icarus and Friends" or
"Mrs. Sadie Adler, Widow": those events follow the mission pages and the fact-checked parts (sadie_A, arthur_B/C,
dutch_B, kieran_A).
Cross-checked against fact-checked parts arthur_B/C, dutch_A/B/C, kieran_A, sadie_A, micah_A, hosea_A, bill_A, susan_A,
molly_A.

The brother and Annabelle: Dutch's own account ("I killed Colm's brother... long time ago... then he killed... a woman I
loved dear", Blessed are the Peacemakers) gives the brother first; the Red Dead Wiki's "Old Friends" mission page gives
the reverse order (brother killed in retaliation for Annabelle). Both accounts are given, attributed, in ONE place:
part B, Relationships > Dutch. The Biography only points to it and states no order. Arthur's "You killed his brother,
Dutch" (Old Friends) gives no order. Why Dutch killed the brother is never explained.
Fact-check fixes (20 Oct 2026): Dutch's "much less fun... if he never finds out" (Old Friends); Pearson met "a couple
of" O'Driscolls; Lenny's remark after the guards are dead; "Colm is going to shit his pants!" quoted (Outlaws l.347);
one guard only "thinks" Colm went to speak to the law; Arthur tortured at Lone Mule Stead (mission page, guard line
"It's one thing torturing a man"), no duration; recovery "a few weeks" (mission page); Tom as Jake's killer = Sadie's
words (mission page), Tom as later leader = wiki-only, attributed; John's "woman-killer" = wiki mission-page trivia,
conditional; letter to Tom told once, in the Widow paragraph. Moved out (duplicates): Dutch and Micah's apologies
(Relationships > Arthur), the Old Friends feud dialogue (Relationships > Dutch), Dutch on Colm's men (Skills), "That
man can really hate" (Personality), "say goodbye to Annabelle" (Relationships > Annabelle), the parley and captivity
lines (Personality, In his own words), the newspaper's crimes list (Personality).
The law, not Milton: in the transcript Colm and his men speak only of "the law" (Colm and Patrick ride into town "to
speak to the law"); the character page says Pinkertons, kept attributed. No source names Andrew Milton in a deal with
Colm: no Milton claim is made. Colm takes no part in the Saint Denis bank job: not mentioned.

Excluded: the FR wiki's "tortured for days", "gagged" and "Dutch mocks him on the gallows" (no other source); the
character page's reading of Colm's terror as "true cowardice" (interpretation); "tertiary antagonist" labels;
the O'Driscoll Boys page's claim that the trap would have ended with Dutch "ultimately killed" (not in the transcript);
"Guiteau Square" for the gallows (only on the gang page); a founding year stated as fact (the 1889 date is the wiki's
deduction from "nearly ten years", given attributed); Kieran's descriptions of Colm, the name pronunciation, the
appearance and weapons (part B); the music theme, cut horse and real-world material (parts C and D).
"""


def two(en, fr): return {"en": en, "fr": fr}




BLOCKS = [
    # ================================================================ Origins
    {"h3": two("Origins", "Origines"), "year": ""},
    {"p": two("The game gives no birth date or birthplace for Colm O'Driscoll. The Red Dead Wiki describes him as an American of Irish descent. According to the same wiki, he and [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]] were at first loosely partnered, before each man led his own gang: the O'Driscoll Boys for Colm, the Van der Linde gang for Dutch. In 1899, the newspaper article \"O'Driscoll Captured\" says that his gang has been active across numerous Western states for nearly ten years. From that figure, the Red Dead Wiki dates the founding of the gang to around 1889. The wiki also states that he was convicted of murder twice and got away both times before he could be hanged.",
              "Le jeu ne donne ni date ni lieu de naissance pour Colm O'Driscoll. Le Red Dead Wiki le présente comme un Américain d'origine irlandaise. Toujours selon ce wiki, [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]] et lui ont d'abord été vaguement associés, avant de diriger chacun sa propre bande : les O'Driscoll Boys pour Colm, la bande Van der Linde pour Dutch. En 1899, l'article de presse \"O'Driscoll Captured\" affirme que sa bande sévit depuis près de dix ans dans de nombreux États de l'Ouest. Le Red Dead Wiki en déduit qu'elle a été fondée vers 1889. Le même wiki précise qu'il a été condamné deux fois pour meurtre et qu'il a filé les deux fois avant d'être pendu.")},
    {"p": two("The feud between the two gangs goes back to two killings: Colm's brother, killed by Dutch, and Annabelle, a woman Dutch loved, killed by Colm. Dutch and the Red Dead Wiki give the two deaths in opposite orders (see Relationships, Dutch van der Linde). By 1899 the two gangs had been fighting over scores for years, as [[arthur-morgan|Arthur Morgan]] explains to [[charles-smith|Charles Smith]] in \"The Aftermath of Genesis\". He describes the O'Driscolls as a big gang and says that Colm and Dutch have known each other a long time, on bad terms. He adds that the Van der Linde gang had barely run into them over the previous six months.",
              "La guerre entre les deux bandes remonte à deux meurtres : celui du frère de Colm, tué par Dutch, et celui d'Annabelle, une femme que Dutch aimait, tuée par Colm. Dutch et le Red Dead Wiki ne placent pas ces deux morts dans le même ordre (voir Relations, Dutch van der Linde). En 1899, cela fait des années que les deux bandes se disputent des coups, comme [[arthur-morgan|Arthur Morgan]] l'explique à [[charles-smith|Charles Smith]] dans \"The Aftermath of Genesis\". Il parle d'une grosse bande et précise que Colm et Dutch se connaissent depuis longtemps, et pas en bons termes. Il ajoute que la bande Van der Linde ne les avait guère croisés au cours des six derniers mois.")},

    # ================================================================ RDR2 1899
    {"h3": two("Red Dead Redemption 2 (1899)", "Red Dead Redemption 2 (1899)"), "year": "1899"},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 1: Colter", "Chapitre 1 : Colter"), "chapter": 1},
    {"p": two("After the failed ferry robbery in Blackwater, the Van der Linde gang hides in the snow of the Grizzlies, where Colm's men are also active. In \"Outlaws from the West\", Dutch, Arthur and [[micah-bell|Micah Bell]] find O'Driscolls occupying the Adler ranch, where they have killed the husband of [[sadie-adler|Sadie Adler]]. One of them recognizes Dutch and shouts to the others: \"Colm is going to shit his pants!\" A shootout follows. Searching the house, Arthur remarks that the bounty on Colm is almost as high as the one on Dutch. Dutch replies that he and Uncle Sam agree on hardly anything except wanting Colm dead. An O'Driscoll caught in the barn tells Arthur that Colm is with the others at an old mining camp to the southwest, near a lake. He adds that they are preparing to rob a train by blowing up the tracks.",
              "Après le braquage raté du ferry de Blackwater, la bande Van der Linde se cache dans la neige des Grizzlies, où les hommes de Colm sont eux aussi présents. Dans \"Outlaws from the West\", Dutch, Arthur et [[micah-bell|Micah Bell]] trouvent des O'Driscoll installés au ranch Adler, où ils ont tué le mari de [[sadie-adler|Sadie Adler]]. L'un d'eux reconnaît Dutch et lance aux autres : \"Colm is going to shit his pants!\" (Colm va chier dans son froc !). Une fusillade éclate. En fouillant la maison, Arthur fait remarquer que la prime sur la tête de Colm est presque aussi élevée que celle de Dutch. Dutch répond que l'Oncle Sam et lui ne s'entendent sur presque rien, sauf sur le fait de vouloir la mort de Colm. Un O'Driscoll surpris dans la grange révèle à Arthur que Colm se trouve avec les autres dans un ancien camp minier au sud-ouest, près d'un lac. Il ajoute qu'ils s'apprêtent à attaquer un train en faisant sauter la voie.")},
    {"p": two("In \"Old Friends\", Dutch breaks up a fight between Micah and [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]], telling them that Colm is the one who needs hitting. He then leads Arthur, Micah, Bill, [[javier-escuella|Javier Escuella]] and [[lenny-summers|Lenny Summers]] to the O'Driscoll camp at Ewing Basin, talking with Arthur about the feud on the way (see Relationships, Dutch van der Linde). From a ridge, Dutch and Arthur watch Colm through binoculars. He calls a young man over, mounts his horse and strikes him. The young man rides away, and Colm's party leaves soon after. Dutch decides that Colm can wait, saying it would be much less fun to rob him and his score if he never found out about it.",
              "Dans \"Old Friends\", Dutch sépare Micah et [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]], qui en viennent aux mains, en leur rappelant que c'est Colm qu'il faudrait frapper. Il emmène ensuite Arthur, Micah, Bill, [[javier-escuella|Javier Escuella]] et [[lenny-summers|Lenny Summers]] vers le camp O'Driscoll d'Ewing Basin, et parle en chemin de la vendetta avec Arthur (voir Relations, Dutch van der Linde). Depuis une crête, Dutch et Arthur observent Colm à la jumelle. Il fait venir un jeune homme, monte à cheval et le frappe. Le jeune homme s'éloigne, et Colm part peu après avec ses hommes. Dutch décide que Colm attendra : ce serait bien moins drôle, dit-il, de lui voler son coup sans qu'il le sache.")},
    {"p": two("The gang kills the men left in the camp, then the reinforcements that come out of the woods. Micah finds the plans for the train robbery, and Arthur finds dynamite. On the way back, Arthur captures the young man Colm had struck, [[kieran-duffy|Kieran Duffy]], who is brought to Colter as a prisoner. In \"Who the Hell is Leviticus Cornwall?\", the gang puts to use what Dutch calls the information kindly provided by the O'Driscolls. It stops the private train of [[leviticus-cornwall|Leviticus Cornwall]] in the Grizzlies and takes the railroad bonds on board. Once the guards are dead, Lenny remarks that he now sees why the O'Driscolls had brought so many men for this job.",
              "La bande abat les hommes restés au camp, puis les renforts qui sortent des bois. Micah trouve les plans de l'attaque du train, et Arthur de la dynamite. Sur le chemin du retour, Arthur capture le jeune homme que Colm avait frappé, [[kieran-duffy|Kieran Duffy]], qui est ramené prisonnier à Colter. Dans \"Who the Hell is Leviticus Cornwall?\", la bande exploite ce que Dutch appelle les renseignements aimablement fournis par les O'Driscoll. Elle arrête dans les Grizzlies le train privé de [[leviticus-cornwall|Leviticus Cornwall]] et s'empare des obligations ferroviaires transportées à bord. Une fois les gardes abattus, Lenny remarque qu'il comprend maintenant pourquoi les O'Driscoll avaient prévu autant d'hommes pour ce coup.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 2: Horseshoe Overlook", "Chapitre 2 : Horseshoe Overlook"), "chapter": 2},
    {"p": two("In \"Paying a Social Call\", Kieran, tied up at the Horseshoe Overlook camp for close to a month, is threatened with gelding. He names Six Point Cabin, in Cumberland Forest, as the place where Colm is holed up. Arthur rides there with Bill and [[john-marston|John Marston]], with Kieran as their guide. According to the Red Dead Wiki's mission page, if the player talks to neither man on the way, John brings up the murder of Annabelle and calls Colm a woman-killer in front of Kieran. The three men kill the O'Driscolls at the hideout, but Colm is not there. Kieran then saves Arthur's life and is allowed to stay with the gang.",
              "Dans \"Paying a Social Call\", Kieran, attaché depuis près d'un mois au camp de Horseshoe Overlook, est menacé de castration. Il désigne Six Point Cabin, dans la forêt de Cumberland, comme la cachette de Colm. Arthur s'y rend avec Bill et [[john-marston|John Marston]], Kieran leur servant de guide. D'après la page de la mission sur le Red Dead Wiki, si le joueur ne parle à aucun des deux en chemin, John évoque le meurtre d'Annabelle et traite Colm de tueur de femmes devant Kieran. Les trois hommes abattent les O'Driscoll de la planque, mais Colm n'y est pas. Kieran sauve ensuite la vie d'Arthur et obtient de rester dans la bande.")},
    {"p": two("Colm's men cross the gang's path twice more in this chapter. In \"Blessed are the Meek?\", Micah, jailed in Strawberry, shoots his O'Driscoll cellmate as he breaks out. In \"An American Pastoral Scene\", a large band of O'Driscolls attacks Arthur and Micah near the Dakota River to take the banking coach the two men have just stolen.",
              "Les hommes de Colm croisent encore deux fois la route du gang pendant ce chapitre. Dans \"Blessed are the Meek?\", Micah, enfermé à Strawberry, abat son codétenu O'Driscoll en s'évadant. Dans \"An American Pastoral Scene\", une grosse troupe d'O'Driscoll attaque Arthur et Micah près de la Dakota River pour leur reprendre la diligence de banque qu'ils viennent de voler.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 3: Clemens Point", "Chapitre 3 : Clemens Point"), "chapter": 3},
    {"p": two("At Clemens Point, in \"Blessed are the Peacemakers\", [[simon-pearson|Simon Pearson]] reports that a couple of O'Driscolls he met on the road into town have suggested a parley to end the feud. [[hosea-matthews|Hosea Matthews]] is against it. Micah grants that it is probably a trap but asks what they have to lose. Dutch agrees to go with Micah, while Arthur covers them with a rifle from higher ground. At the meeting point, Colm mocks Dutch's leadership and asks about the score the gang stole from him. He then says that he has been offered a price to bring Dutch in, and that he might still take it. Their exchange is quoted under Personality.",
              "À Clemens Point, dans \"Blessed are the Peacemakers\", [[simon-pearson|Simon Pearson]] raconte que deux ou trois O'Driscoll croisés sur la route de la ville ont proposé des pourparlers pour mettre fin à la querelle. [[hosea-matthews|Hosea Matthews]] s'y oppose. Micah reconnaît qu'il s'agit sans doute d'un piège, mais demande ce qu'ils ont à perdre. Dutch accepte d'y aller avec Micah, pendant qu'Arthur les couvre au fusil depuis une hauteur. Au point de rendez-vous, Colm se moque de la façon dont Dutch mène sa bande et lui demande des nouvelles du coup qu'on lui a volé. Il annonce ensuite qu'on lui a proposé une somme pour livrer Dutch, et qu'il pourrait encore accepter. Leur échange est cité dans la rubrique Personnalité.")},
    {"p": two("While the two men talk, O'Driscolls creep up on Arthur, knock him out and carry him off. He wakes up wounded at Lone Mule Stead, in Big Valley, where the O'Driscolls hold him prisoner and torture him. One guard thinks that Colm has gone into town with a man named Patrick to speak to the law. Another says that Colm is right and that Arthur will draw the whole Van der Linde gang to them; he also blames the gang for the death of a man called Seamus. Colm then comes down to see Arthur. He offers him a place in his gang and accuses him of killing many of his men at Six Point Cabin, which Arthur denies.",
              "Pendant que les deux hommes parlent, des O'Driscoll surprennent Arthur, l'assomment et l'emmènent. Il se réveille blessé à Lone Mule Stead, dans Big Valley, où les O'Driscoll le retiennent prisonnier et le torturent. L'un des gardiens croit savoir que Colm est parti en ville avec un certain Patrick pour parler à la loi. Un autre estime que Colm a raison et qu'Arthur leur amènera toute la bande Van der Linde ; il reproche aussi au gang la mort d'un certain Seamus. Colm descend ensuite voir Arthur. Il lui propose de rejoindre sa bande et l'accuse d'avoir tué bon nombre de ses hommes à Six Point Cabin, ce qu'Arthur nie.")},
    {"p": two("Arthur urges Colm to let him go and end the feud, since both gangs now have bigger problems. Colm answers that once they have Dutch, they will forget about him. He then reveals his plan: Dutch will come to rescue Arthur, the O'Driscolls will capture them all and hand them over to the law waiting for them, and then vanish. He admits that the parley was only a way to seize Arthur. The character page of the Red Dead Wiki says that Colm had made this deal with the Pinkertons; in the mission itself, Colm and his men speak only of the law. Once Colm has left, Arthur frees himself, kills a guard and escapes on horseback. He reaches Clemens Point and collapses. [[mary-beth-gaskill|Mary-Beth Gaskill]], [[karen-jones|Karen Jones]] and Dutch find him, and he tells Dutch that Colm was going to set the law on them. His recovery takes a few weeks.",
              "Arthur presse Colm de le relâcher et d'enterrer la querelle, puisque les deux bandes ont désormais de plus gros soucis. Colm répond qu'une fois Dutch entre leurs mains, on l'oubliera, lui. Il dévoile alors son plan : Dutch viendra délivrer Arthur, les O'Driscoll les captureront tous, les livreront à la loi qui les attendra sur place, puis disparaîtront. Il reconnaît que les pourparlers n'avaient pour but que de s'emparer d'Arthur. La fiche du personnage sur le Red Dead Wiki affirme que Colm avait passé cet accord avec les Pinkerton ; dans la mission, Colm et ses hommes ne parlent que de la loi. Une fois Colm parti, Arthur se libère, tue un garde et s'enfuit à cheval. Il atteint Clemens Point et s'effondre. [[mary-beth-gaskill|Mary-Beth Gaskill]], [[karen-jones|Karen Jones]] et Dutch le découvrent, et il explique à Dutch que Colm comptait leur mettre la loi sur le dos. Sa convalescence dure quelques semaines.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 4: Saint Denis", "Chapitre 4 : Saint-Denis"), "chapter": 4},
    {"p": two("Colm does not appear in person in this chapter, but his gang strikes the Van der Linde camp at Shady Belle. Kieran disappears after the party held for the return of [[jack-marston|Jack Marston]]. In \"Horsemen, Apocalypses\", his horse carries him back into camp dead: the O'Driscolls have beheaded him, gouged out his eyes and set his head in his own hands. A large band of O'Driscolls attacks Shady Belle at once. The gang falls back into the house and holds it, and the surviving attackers flee.",
              "Colm n'apparaît pas en personne dans ce chapitre, mais sa bande frappe le camp Van der Linde à Shady Belle. Kieran disparaît après la fête donnée pour le retour de [[jack-marston|Jack Marston]]. Dans \"Horsemen, Apocalypses\", son cheval le ramène au camp, mort : les O'Driscoll l'ont décapité, lui ont crevé les yeux et ont posé sa tête entre ses mains. Une grosse troupe d'O'Driscoll attaque aussitôt Shady Belle. La bande se retranche dans la maison et tient bon, et les assaillants encore en vie prennent la fuite.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 6: Beaver Hollow", "Chapitre 6 : Beaver Hollow"), "chapter": 6},
    {"p": two("Colm is arrested while the gang is camped at Beaver Hollow. The newspaper article \"O'Driscoll Captured\" reports that a deputy caught him during a routine coach inspection. Judge Taylor examined him the next day, and he was sentenced to hang for murder in Saint Denis. In \"Icarus and Friends\", Arthur rescues Sadie from O'Driscolls chasing her near Annesburg, and she tells him the news. Arthur points out that Colm has escaped before. Sadie answers that she means to make sure he does not get away this time.",
              "Colm est arrêté pendant que la bande campe à Beaver Hollow. L'article \"O'Driscoll Captured\" rapporte qu'un adjoint du shérif l'a pris lors d'un contrôle de routine d'une diligence. Le juge Taylor l'a entendu dès le lendemain, et il a été condamné à être pendu pour meurtre à Saint-Denis. Dans \"Icarus and Friends\", Arthur tire Sadie des griffes d'O'Driscoll qui la poursuivent près d'Annesburg, et elle lui annonce la nouvelle. Arthur rappelle que Colm s'est déjà évadé. Sadie répond qu'elle compte bien s'assurer qu'il n'en réchappe pas cette fois.")},
    {"p": two("In \"Goodbye, Dear Friend\", Dutch and Sadie decide to attend the hanging, because Colm has already escaped the noose twice, and they bring Arthur. Dutch and Arthur go disguised as Saint Denis policemen, and Sadie dresses as a society lady. Before the execution, Dutch reminds Sadie of what each of them has lost because of Colm: her husband, his Annabelle, and Kieran. Near the gallows, the three spot two O'Driscolls in the crowd. Dutch and Arthur follow one of them and overhear the rescue plan. Arthur deals with Paul, a sniper posted on a rooftop facing the gallows, and takes his place with the rifle. Dutch and Sadie each hold an O'Driscoll at gunpoint in the crowd.",
              "Dans \"Goodbye, Dear Friend\", Dutch et Sadie décident d'assister à la pendaison, puisque Colm a déjà échappé deux fois à la corde, et emmènent Arthur. Dutch et Arthur se déguisent en policiers de Saint-Denis, et Sadie s'habille en dame de la bonne société. Avant l'exécution, Dutch rappelle à Sadie ce que chacun d'eux a perdu à cause de Colm : elle son mari, lui son Annabelle, et Kieran. Près de la potence, tous trois repèrent deux O'Driscoll dans la foule. Dutch et Arthur suivent l'un d'eux et surprennent le plan d'évasion. Arthur règle son compte à Paul, un tireur posté sur un toit face à la potence, et prend sa place avec le fusil. Dutch et Sadie tiennent chacun un O'Driscoll en joue dans la foule.")},
    {"p": two("On the gallows, Colm at first looks confident that his men will save him. He then sees them held at gunpoint and looks in turn at Dutch, at Sadie and at Arthur, on the roof in place of his sniper. The Red Dead Wiki gives his last words as: \"As well you may. I've been a bad man. These charges...\" Colm is hanged. Sadie then kills both hostages, which starts a shootout with the remaining O'Driscolls and with the city's lawmen. Arthur covers Dutch and Sadie from the roof, and the three get back to camp.",
              "Sur l'échafaud, Colm semble d'abord certain que ses hommes vont le sauver. Il les voit ensuite tenus en joue et regarde tour à tour Dutch, Sadie et Arthur, posté sur le toit à la place de son tireur. Le Red Dead Wiki rapporte ainsi ses dernières paroles : \"As well you may. I've been a bad man. These charges...\" (libre à vous ; j'ai été un homme mauvais ; ces accusations...). Colm est pendu. Sadie abat alors les deux otages, ce qui déclenche une fusillade avec les derniers O'Driscoll, puis avec les forces de l'ordre de la ville. Arthur couvre Dutch et Sadie depuis le toit, et tous trois regagnent le camp.")},
    {"p": two("The gang Colm leaves behind does not last long. In \"Mrs. Sadie Adler, Widow\", Sadie finds the last O'Driscolls at Hanging Dog Ranch, in Big Valley. Arthur first says he no longer cares about them since Colm's hanging. If he agrees to go, the two wipe out the gang. Sadie kills the last of them, Tom, whom she names as the man who killed her husband. According to the Red Dead Wiki, Tom had led the gang since Colm's death.",
              "La bande que laisse Colm ne lui survit guère. Dans \"Mrs. Sadie Adler, Widow\", Sadie retrouve les derniers O'Driscoll à Hanging Dog Ranch, dans Big Valley. Arthur commence par dire que les O'Driscoll ne l'intéressent plus depuis la pendaison de Colm. S'il accepte de l'accompagner, tous deux anéantissent la bande. Sadie tue le dernier d'entre eux, Tom, qu'elle désigne comme le meurtrier de son mari. Selon le Red Dead Wiki, Tom dirigeait la bande depuis la mort de Colm.")},
    {"p": two("Tom carries a letter Colm wrote him from his cell in Saint Denis. Colm says that he is held apart from the main jail, on the other side of town, in a small room with a big door and many guards working in shifts. He would pass on the guards' names and addresses if he knew them. He expects people in the crowd at his execution to call for his blood, and hopes to see a few friendly faces as well. He writes that prison has given him time to think about his past, some of which he regrets and some of which he does not. He was caught, he explains, in the bed of a disloyal, loud-mouthed woman. He asks Tom to visit her, to tell her that all is forgiven and perhaps to leave her something lasting to remember him by.",
              "Tom porte sur lui une lettre que Colm lui a écrite depuis sa cellule de Saint-Denis. Colm y explique qu'on le garde à l'écart de la prison principale, à l'autre bout de la ville, dans une petite pièce fermée par une grosse porte, sous la surveillance de nombreux gardiens qui se relaient. S'il connaissait leurs noms et leurs adresses, il les transmettrait. Il s'attend à ce que des gens réclament son sang dans la foule le jour de son exécution, et espère y voir aussi quelques visages amis. La prison, écrit-il, lui a laissé le temps de repenser à ses actes : il en regrette certains, pas d'autres. Il raconte s'être fait prendre dans le lit d'une femme déloyale et bavarde. Il demande à Tom de rendre visite à cette femme, de lui dire que tout est pardonné et, peut-être, de lui laisser de quoi se souvenir de lui pour longtemps.")},
    {"p": two("By 1907, according to the Red Dead Wiki, some of the gang's former hideouts are held by the Laramie Gang. In the ending in which Arthur goes back for the money with low honor, as Micah stabs him, Arthur begs Dutch to see that Micah, not [[molly-oshea|Molly]], [[susan-grimshaw|Miss Grimshaw]] or even Colm, is the informant.",
              "En 1907, selon le Red Dead Wiki, plusieurs anciennes planques de la bande sont occupées par le gang Laramie. Dans la fin où Arthur retourne chercher l'argent avec un honneur bas, alors que Micah le poignarde, Arthur supplie Dutch de comprendre que le mouchard est Micah, et non [[molly-oshea|Molly]], [[susan-grimshaw|Miss Grimshaw]] ou même Colm.")},
]
